It is twelve o'clock.
It is lunch time.
Peter and I go down to the canteen.
The canteen is large and bright.
We are very hungry.
We look at the good food.
There are many options today.
I choose a classic open sandwich.
It is with fish and lemon.
Peter takes a large salad.
We walk over to the register.
The clerk gives us two plates.
"That will be forty kroner," he says to me.
I pay with my card.
"Here you go," I say.
"Thank you, and enjoy your meal," he answers.
We find a table by the window.
We sit down.
The food tastes really good.
It is a cozy break.
